🧭 12-Month Low-Level Systems & Embedded Roadmap

🎯 Goal: Build deep understanding of CPUs, OS, firmware, and virtualization to become a strong Firmware / Kernel / Embedded Engineer.

🩵 Months 1 – 3: CPU & Embedded Foundations

Goal: Master computer architecture basics and embedded C/ASM.

📘 Study

- [ ] Read Computer Organization & Design — Patterson & Hennessy
- [ ] Review caches, pipelines, memory hierarchy, interrupts
- [ ] Learn basic x86 and ARM assembly
- [ ] Study CPU identification: cpuid, registers, MSRs

🧰 Practice

- [ ] Explore your system with cpuid, lscpu, dmidecode, perf
- [ ] Write simple assembly (Fibonacci, memory copy, I/O port)
- [ ] Blink an LED on STM32 or Raspberry Pi Pico (bare-metal C)

🧩 Mini Project

 - [ ] System Information Tool: read and display CPU info using cpuid and C.

⚙️ Months 4 – 6: Operating Systems & Low-Level Programming

Goal: Understand OS interaction with hardware.

📘 Study

 - [ ] Read Modern Operating Systems — Tanenbaum
 - [ ] Learn Linux kernel basics: processes, interrupts, scheduling
 - [ ] Explore kernel source (arch/x86/, drivers/)

🧰 Practice

 - [ ] Write a Linux kernel module (character device driver)
 - [ ] Explore /proc and /sys filesystem
 - [ ] Use gdb, objdump, strace, and perf for debugging

🧩 Mini Project

 - [ ] Kernel Module: read CPU MSRs using inline assembly.

🧠 Months 7 – 9: Firmware, Boot & Virtualization

- [ ] Goal: Learn firmware, boot process, and hypervisor concepts.

📘 Study

 - [ ] Understand BIOS → UEFI → OS boot flow
 - [ ] Learn ACPI tables, memory maps
 - [ ] Study Intel VT-x / AMD-V, EPT, VMCS
 - [ ] Read about QEMU, KVM, Coreboot, EDK2

🧰 Practice

 - [ ] Build and boot Coreboot or EDK2 in a VM
 - [ ] Write a simple bootloader in C + ASM
 - [ ] Experiment with QEMU: trap and emulate instructions

🧩 Mini Project

 - [ ] Minimal Hypervisor Demo: trap cpuid or port I/O inside a VM.

🔧 Months 10 – 12: Specialization & Portfolio

Goal: Apply knowledge to a focused real-world project.

Choose one path:
💡 Option A – Embedded Firmware

 - [ ] Implement I²C/SPI/UART drivers from scratch
 - [ ] Port and configure FreeRTOS / Zephyr on an MCU
 - [ ] Project: Custom sensor board with RTOS + communication stack

🧩 Option B – Kernel / Virtualization

 - [ ] Extend or modify a Linux driver/scheduler
 - [ ] Build tools using libvirt + C to manage VMs
 - [ ] Project: Virtual CPU feature inspector or sandbox

🔐 Option C – Hardware Security

 - [ ] Study Spectre/Meltdown, CET, SGX, TrustZone
 - [ ] Perform timing-attack or side-channel experiments
 - [ ] Project: Secure enclave or timing-attack demo

📚 Resources

 - [ ] 🎓 Nand2Tetris — computer-from-scratch course
 - [ ] 🎓 MIT 6.S081 Operating Systems Engineering (YouTube + labs)
 - [ ] 🎓 Georgia Tech – Intro to Computer Architecture
 - [ ] 📄 Intel Software Developer Manuals (Vol 1–3)
 - [ ] 🧰 Tools: QEMU, GDB, perf, MSR-tools, Coreboot, EDK2, Docker

🧱 Final Deliverables

 - [ ] 🧠 Write a blog/GitHub documentation for each stage
 - [ ] 💻 2–3 working projects (bare-metal, driver, or hypervisor)

 
 
 📄 Updated résumé highlighting “Low-Level Systems Development”




