## Quarter 1 – CPU & Embedded Foundations (Weeks 1–13)

### Week 1
- [ ] Read Chapter 1 of *Computer Organization & Design* (basic CPU structure)
- [ ] Explore your CPU using `lscpu` or `cpuid`
- [ ] Write a “Hello World” in C on your MCU

### Week 2
- [ ] Study CPU registers and instruction sets (x86 basics)
- [ ] Write simple assembly (add, sub, move instructions)
- [ ] Blink an LED on STM32 or Raspberry Pi Pico

### Week 3
- [ ] Learn memory hierarchy: cache, RAM, registers
- [ ] Write assembly for memory load/store operations
- [ ] Explore memory layout of a small C program using `objdump`

### Week 4
- [ ] Understand CPU pipelines and instruction execution
- [ ] Write small performance-sensitive C code and measure cycles
- [ ] Mini Project: Print CPU info (vendor, cores, cache)

### Week 5
- [ ] Study interrupts and exceptions in CPU
- [ ] Write a basic interrupt handler in bare-metal C
- [ ] Simulate a hardware interrupt with a button on MCU

### Week 6
- [ ] Learn ARM assembly basics
- [ ] Port previous assembly programs to ARM
- [ ] Compare instruction timings between x86 and ARM

### Week 7
- [ ] Study I/O ports and memory-mapped I/O
- [ ] Access GPIO registers on MCU using C
- [ ] Mini Project: Control LED via memory-mapped I/O

### Week 8
- [ ] Understand CPU modes (user/kernel/system)
- [ ] Explore Linux `/proc/cpuinfo` for modes and features
- [ ] Inline assembly in C to read CPU flags

### Week 9
- [ ] Study CPU features (MSRs, SIMD, virtualization flags)
- [ ] Experiment with reading MSRs on Linux using `msr-tools`
- [ ] Write simple SIMD operations in C/ASM

### Week 10
- [ ] Review pipelines, hazards, branch prediction
- [ ] Write C code to test branch prediction behavior
- [ ] Mini Project: Small benchmark program in C

### Week 11
- [ ] Study power management and CPU frequency scaling
- [ ] Explore `/sys/devices/system/cpu` in Linux
- [ ] Change CPU frequency and observe performance

### Week 12
- [ ] Review all assembly, CPU, and memory topics
- [ ] Consolidate mini projects into a small “CPU Explorer” program
- [ ] Document findings in Markdown

### Week 13
- [ ] Test embedded knowledge by writing a small bare-metal project
- [ ] Blink multiple LEDs using timers and interrupts
- [ ] Submit first quarter mini-project for self-assessment

---

## Quarter 2 – Operating Systems & Low-Level Programming (Weeks 14–26)

### Week 14
- [ ] Start *Modern Operating Systems* (Tanenbaum) Chapter 1–2
