### Week 16
- [ ] Learn memory management: virtual memory, paging
- [ ] Explore `/proc/self/maps` for process memory layout
- [ ] Experiment with `mmap` in C

### Week 17
- [ ] Study Linux kernel modules (loading/unloading)
- [ ] Write a char device driver
- [ ] Test the driver with simple read/write operations

### Week 18
- [ ] Explore kernel synchronization primitives (spinlocks, mutexes)
- [ ] Modify driver to handle concurrent access
- [ ] Mini Project: Thread-safe kernel module

### Week 19
